        <title type="html"><![CDATA[ShadowRoot.innerHTML - update to support TrustedHTML]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40790</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40790"/>
        <updated>2025-08-19T18:31:35.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">This updates <code class="notranslate">ShadowRoot.innerHTML</code> property to the pattern we're using to document the need for trusted types on injection sinks.</p>
<p dir="auto">This doc is virtually a copy of the <code class="notranslate">Element.innerHTML</code>. The differences are because this is a shadow root.</p>
<p dir="auto">The one thing I omitted I think might be relevant was <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/innerHTML#shadow_dom_considerations" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/innerHTML#shadow_dom_considerations</a> - I suspect it is true because the algorithms are virtually the same -  but I couldn't verify from the spec.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work is being tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2770544982" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/37518/hovercard?comment_id=2629763658&amp;comment_type=issue_comment" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518#issuecomment-2629763658">#37518 (comment)</a></p>]]></content>
